-- title:
--   Degree-zero vectors are torsion modulo graph Laplacian rows
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $n$, $m$, maps $\mathrm{src}, \mathrm{tgt} : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ describing the endpoints of the $m$ edges of a multigraph on $n$ vertices, and weights $W : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathbb{N}$ with $W(e) > 0$ for all $e$. Assume the cut form of connectedness: for every finite set $S$ of vertices with $S$ and its complement both nonempty there is an edge $e$ with $\mathrm{src}(e) \in S$ if and only if $\mathrm{tgt}(e) \notin S$, i.e. an edge meeting $S$ in exactly one endpoint. Let $V = \mathrm{Fin}\,n \sqcup \{(e,i) : i < W(e)-1\}$ be the vertex set of the graph in which edge $e$ is subdivided into $W(e)$ segments, the segments being indexed by pairs $(e,i)$ with $i < W(e)$ and having endpoints $\mathrm{src}(e)$ or $(e,i-1)$ according as $i = 0$ or not, and $\mathrm{tgt}(e)$ or $(e,i)$ according as $i+1 = W(e)$ or not. For $v \in V$ let $\mathrm{lap}(v) \in \mathbb{Z}^{V}$ be the sum, over all segments having $v$ as an endpoint, of $\delta_v$ minus the indicator of the other endpoint of that segment (counted once for each of the two ends, so that loops contribute zero). The conclusion is that every $x : V \to \mathbb{Z}$ with $\sum_{v} x(v) = 0$ has finite order in the quotient of $\mathbb{Z}^{V}$ by the additive subgroup generated by the vectors $\mathrm{lap}(v)$, $v \in V$.
--
--   This is the statement that the degree-zero part of $\mathbb{Z}^{V}$ modulo the image of the combinatorial Laplacian of a connected graph is torsion, the torsion quotient being the critical (sandpile) group of the subdivided graph. It is used in the component-group computation attached to a semistable covering, where the Laplacian relations come from the intersection matrix of the dual graph of a semistable model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_SemistableCovering_isOfFinAddOrder_mk_quotient_lap_of_sum_eq_zero_of_forall_exists_src_mem_iff.lean

